  "observations": {
    "wallpaper": "GDI hidden guard; stored downscale factor<2 selects BitBlt, otherwise StretchBlt. OGL screen-space Push2dProjection, depth-write disable and glDrawPixels paths; viewport/clip rectangle path can use temporary DIB and StretchBlt before drawing. Raw blit/raster coordinates and GL parameter arguments require ABI/disassembly refinement.",
    "trace": "GDI hidden guard, source plane and width/height passed as intervals[0,width],[0,height] to DrawTexturedPlane after cache lookup. OGL hidden guard; skips when both extents zero; one zero extent derives from loaded texture aspect. Quad corners use Plane.PointAt(0,0),(0,height),(width,height),(width,0). Texture-manager lookup includes filename and gray mode. Missing texture has an actual diagnostic quad/text branch; do not invent successful rendering or silently omit it.",
    "traceGetImage": "Active-document table Bitmap(filename,true) then actual Dib; if gray flag calls ConvertToGrayScale; missing document/table/decode fails false. OGL texture manager is separate; equivalence is unproven.",
    "traceGrayscale": "Separate ConvertToGrayScale first calls IncreaseColorDepth(24). For24bit iterates pixel width per row using storage stride, leaving padding; adds0.5 before truncation. 32bit branch writes computed gray to all FOUR bytes including alpha. Same0.299/0.589/0.111 constants, but this is not wallpaper flat-storage truncation. Source IncreaseColorDepth conversion and OGL gray-cache internals remain unresolved.",
    "pipeline": "Both exported pipeline methods have configuration/override branches; normal path delegates via engine virtual call. Override DIB/copy code has unresolved effective output behavior. Ghidra opaque class-scaled offsets and dropped imported GL arguments must not be treated as a complete raw layout/render specification."
  },
  "remaining": [
    "Apply explicit GL/BitBlt/StretchBlt ABIs and verify all texture-coordinate/filter/blend/depth/crop arguments",
